{"name":"Kunzite","hex":"#ddb6c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kunzite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pink- to lilac-colored gemstone, a variety of spodumene."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kunzite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spodumene","blocks":[{"text":"Spodumene is a pyroxene mineral consisting of lithium aluminium inosilicate, LiAl(SiO3)2, and is a commercially important source of lithium. It occurs as colorless to yellowish, purplish, or lilac kunzite (see below), or alternatively yellowish-green or emerald-green hiddenite; it takes the form of prismatic crystals, often of great size. Single crystals of 14.3 m (47 ft) in size are reported from the Black Hills of South Dakota, United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Spodumene-usa59abg.jpg/330px-Spodumene-usa59abg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spodumene","wikidata":"Q120547"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Spodumene.jpg/250px-Spodumene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Spodumene.jpg/500px-Spodumene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Spodumene.jpg/250px-Spodumene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpodumene.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Kunzite_Nouristan.jpg/250px-Kunzite_Nouristan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Kunzite_Nouristan.jpg/500px-Kunzite_Nouristan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"htt